@Helen Wright I’m glad they programmed it to allow empty, a space, or rebus “BLANK” for those tiles, because each solver would think of different ways to enter it.

This is the first Thursday I’ve solved without having to look something up, so I guess it was easier than normal.

I had no idea who made Scrabble, so when I got “BUTTS”, i was rather skeptical!

@Rich in Atlanta
Looked it up and solved it--fun!

At first a little annoyed it wouldn't let me leave those squares blank, but then remembered that for older ones, they didn't provide as many rebus options.

@Charles Peterson
What really annoys me is that scrabble now allows “ok.”  This is NOT “okay” or “OK” in my household.  Ok is not a work.  It’s a guttural sound…I would also like for Apple to stop with that being the default response on my watch when I want to respond to a text message using that device, especially since I never use it and I would think that it would “learn” that by now.


As for “ZA,” I would also agree that that isn’t a word…I understand that language is fluid, but the only time I’ve seen/heard that as a substitute for pizza is ironically and uttered with an eye roll.

